Libraries Used

• No external libraries are required for these tasks. All functionality uses the built-in Arduino core framework.

Commands Used in Arduino IDE

• Serial.begin(speed): Initializes serial communication at a specified baud rate.
• Serial.println(text): Prints text data to the Serial Monitor followed by a new line.
• delay(ms): Pauses program execution for a specified duration in milliseconds.
• pinMode(pin, mode): Configures a specific digital pin as an INPUT or OUTPUT.
• digitalWrite(pin, value): Sets a digital pin to HIGH (on) or LOW (off).
• analogRead(pin): Reads the voltage level from a specified analog input pin.
